Here is an interesting offer for a postdoc position. The closing date is very soon, however!

Subject: Postdoc position in evolutionary ecology

** Caution: EXTERNAL Sender **

Hi,

I have a 3.5 year postdoc position advertised (funded by UK NERC).

The aim is to quantify spatio-temporal variation in selection on seasonal migration, using multi-year multi-location capture-mark-recapture data from a partially migratory bird meta-population (European shags). The post is part of a wider project on eco-evolutionary dynamics in seasonally mobile systems.

It would suit someone who’s interested in the interfaces between population ecology, evolutionary ecology, movement ecology and demography, and who could enjoy getting tangled up in Bayesian capture-mark-recapture…

It’s based at University of Aberdeen (UK), but also with time spent at NTNU (Norway).

I would very much appreciate if you could circulate and flag up to anyone who might be interested (details below, closing date July 15 2024).

Many thanks for your help and best wishes,

Jane

Postdoctoral Research Fellow position in Evolutionary Ecology.

Estimating spatio-temporal variation in selection on seasonal migration, using multi-year multi-location capture-mark-recapture data from a partially migratory bird population.

Based at University of Aberdeen, UK, with some time spent at NTNU, Norway, collaborating with UK Centre for Ecology & Hydrology.

Fully funded for 3.5 years, by UK Natural Environment Research Council.

https://www.abdnjobs.co.uk/vacancy/research-fellow--559960.html

Closing date for applications: July 15th 2024.

Please contact Jane Reid if you are interested or for further information (jane....@ntnu.no or jane...@abdn.ac.uk)

